{
  "id": "c1-e34-development-or-wildlife",
  "level": "C1",
  "version": 1,
  "topic": "Development or wildlife?",
  "parts": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "title": "Interview",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p1-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Good afternoon. First of all, we'd like to know a little about you.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p1-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4500
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q1",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "text": "Candidate A, how important is it for you to live near nature?",
          "durationSec": 25,
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p1-q1.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4500
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q2",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "text": "Candidate B, what kind of nature is there in your area?",
          "durationSec": 25,
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p1-q2.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4300
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q3",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "text": "Candidate A, have you ever been involved in protecting the environment?",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p1-q3.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5100
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q4",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "text": "Candidate B, do you think people in cities are too distant from nature?",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p1-q4.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5200
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "title": "Long turn",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p2-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "In this part of the test, I'm going to give each of you three pictures. I'd like you to talk about two of them on your own for about a minute, and also to answer a question briefly about your partner's pictures.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p2-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 13200
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-a",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "assets": [
            "c1-e34-a1",
            "c1-e34-a2",
            "c1-e34-a3"
          ],
          "text": "Candidate A, your pictures show human activity affecting the natural world. Choose two of the pictures and say what the people involved might be trying to achieve, and what the consequences for wildlife could be.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p2-a.mp3",
          "audioMs": 14300
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-a-follow",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "text": "Candidate B, which of these situations do you find the most worrying?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p2-a-follow.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5200
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-b",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "assets": [
            "c1-e34-b1",
            "c1-e34-b2",
            "c1-e34-b3"
          ],
          "text": "Candidate B, your pictures show people living and working near nature. Choose two of the pictures and say what the relationship between people and nature might be like here, and what conflicts could arise.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p2-b.mp3",
          "audioMs": 13600
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-b-follow",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "text": "Candidate A, how can people and wildlife live side by side?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p2-b-follow.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4900
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "title": "Collaborative task",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p3-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Now I'd like you to talk about something together for about two minutes. Here are some ways in which countries try to protect natural areas while allowing development, and a question for you to discuss.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p3-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 13000
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-discuss",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 120,
          "diagram": "c1-e34-development-or-wildlife",
          "text": "Talk to each other about this question: How might these approaches help to balance development and nature?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p3-discuss.mp3",
          "audioMs": 7200
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-decide",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "diagram": "c1-e34-development-or-wildlife",
          "text": "Now you have about a minute to decide together. Which would be the most workable?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p3-decide.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5500
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "title": "Discussion",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p4-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Now I'd like to ask you some more questions about wildlife and development.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p4-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5600
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q1",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 50,
          "text": "Is economic development more important than protecting wildlife?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p4-q1.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5000
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q2",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate A, should rich countries pay poorer ones to preserve their rainforests?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p4-q2.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5700
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q3",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate B, to what extent should local people have a say in decisions about nearby nature reserves?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p4-q3.mp3",
          "audioMs": 7500
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q4",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 50,
          "text": "Do you think it is possible for tourism to be good for wildlife?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p4-q4.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4700
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q5",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate A, why do some species attract more attention than others?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p4-q5.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4900
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q6",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate B, could new technology help to protect endangered animals?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e34-development-or-wildlife/p4-q6.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5400
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
